  "_read": "Liquid Glass pack, replicated from refs/glass/reference.png (design-contracts/glass.md): the whole page stands on a soft photographic wash; a dark centred pill carries section words with a LIGHT active segment and a light search knob; the wordmark floats white at left, one frosted household pill at right (no bell — no notifications feature); two UNEQUAL tinted glass plates — steel-blue 741 beside periwinkle 1067 — with white titles anchored top-left, dark-disc Play bottom-left, key art bleeding from the facing edge, hairline specular rims and inner sheens instead of drop shadows; frost chips (icon + label) jump to the household's real shelves; rails caption posters below the art with an accent-dot rating line. An original Scenix composition; no marks or assets copied from the reference. Glass surfaces are real lenses, not tinted rectangles: the rim bends and blurs the wall and artwork behind it (frostBevel band, frostRefr bend, frostFall falloff, frostDisp spectral fringe), and the same material carries frostTint/frostBlur/frostSat/frostAberr/frostEdge on the blur tier older televisions run. The wash underneath sits on the pack canvas rather than above it, so the glass has something to be glass against.",
